& [Fold1Identity] names a transport seam rather than a runtime
  + CoordinationToolContext contains the six exact objects already admitted by the checkpoint core
  + CoordinationToolRequest selects BEGIN or ADVANCE and carries every value needed for a pure call
  + CoordinationToolResponse reports a typed status result or fault and explicit nonclaims
  + no adapter-owned session authority exists

& [Fold2Form] keeps machine exchange closed and inspectable
  + context request response status operation result and fault forms reject unknown JSON fields and generate schemas
  + BEGIN carries context only while ADVANCE additionally carries one checkpoint and positive step quota
  + success contains exactly the core checkpoint or transition rather than a paraphrase
  + fault contains stable category code message and no successor value

& [Fold3Dispatch] delegates without reinterpretation
  + BEGIN calls begin_coordination_checkpoint with the six exact context values
  + ADVANCE calls advance_coordination_checkpoint with the same context checkpoint and quota
  + core EvaluationFault category and message are copied into transport fault material
  + equal requests produce byte-equal responses and no external effect

& [Fold4MCP] exposes one ordinary between-pass tool
  + a local STDIO server advertises exactly step_procedure_coordination
  + the tool accepts the transport-neutral request and returns the complete response in structuredContent
  + text content is only a short nonauthoritative operator summary
  + metadata declares read-only idempotent closed-world behavior and the ingress ceiling is finite

& [Fold5InferenceFlow] is host model tool host model
  + a host sends a model prompt containing the small Cantor primer and available tool schema
  + the model or deterministic host emits one tool request between generation passes
  + Cantor validates and advances bounded executable state
  + the host appends the structured response as tool material and starts the next model pass
  + no token hidden-state or KV-cache mutation is required or claimed

& [Fold6Proof] compares adapter and core directly
  + direct BEGIN response equals begin_coordination_checkpoint
  + direct ADVANCE response equals advance_coordination_checkpoint and can reach the proven terminal outcome
  + malformed JSON unknown fields zero quota lineage faults and oversized MCP input fail closed
  + an official RMCP client proves initialization discovery invocation and shutdown against a real subprocess

& [Fold7Boundary] prevents prototype singularity
  + no provider call prompt injection tool registration process-local custody persistence authentication external effect UI or deployment is authorized
  + no existing procedure command schema is silently expanded
  + no claim is made that models will reliably choose the tool without host policy evaluation
  + llama.cpp modification and mid-generation semantic insertion remain deferred

& [PrunedAlternatives] preserves one semantic authority
  - do not rebuild checkpoint validation in the adapter
  - do not place static context in hidden server globals
  - do not treat tool text as authoritative data
  - do not couple the transport-neutral dispatcher to MCP types

& [SelectedFlow] is strict request -> pure core dispatch -> strict response -> structured MCP transport -> later model pass

